The backup/restore flow isn’t protected against unexpected exceptions (e.g., `rename`, `Bun.spawn` failing because `opencode` isn’t on PATH, or stream reads throwing). If an exception happens after moving `UPCOMING_CHANGELOG.md` to `.bak`, the script will exit early and leave the repo with `UPCOMING_CHANGELOG.md` missing and only the `.bak` file. Wrap the move/spawn/exit-code handling in a `try { ... } finally { ... }` (or equivalent) so the original file is restored on any failure path.
```suggestion
let out = ""
let err = ""
let code = 1
let success = false

try {
  const proc = Bun.spawn(["opencode", "run", "--command", "changelog", "--", ...args], {
    cwd: root,
    stdin: "inherit",
    stdout: quiet ? "pipe" : "inherit",
    stderr: quiet ? "pipe" : "inherit",
  })

  if (quiet) {
    ;[out, err] = await Promise.all([
      new Response(proc.stdout).text(),
      new Response(proc.stderr).text(),
    ])
  }

  code = await proc.exited

  if (code === 0) {
    success = true
    if (values.print) {
      process.stdout.write(await Bun.file(file).text())
    }
  } else if (quiet) {
    if (out) process.stdout.write(out)
    if (err) process.stderr.write(err)
  }
} finally {
  if (moved) {
    if (success) {
      await rm(bak, { force: true })
    } else {
      // Restore the original file on any failure path
      await rm(file, { force: true }).catch(() => {})
      await rename(bak, file).catch(() => {})
    }
  }
```

