`runTask()` can throw (e.g., `ctx.ask(...)` rejection/throw, `Session.create`, `MessageV2.get`, `SessionPrompt.resolvePromptParts`, etc.). When that happens, the task's resolver is never resolved and any dependents will wait forever on `await resolvers.get(dep)!.promise`, potentially deadlocking the entire `team` execution. Wrap the task body in `try/catch/finally` so the task state is marked failed/skipped, the resolver is always resolved, and the semaphore is always released.
```suggestion
        try {
          await ctx.ask({
            permission: "task",
            patterns: [t.subagent_type],
            always: ["*"],
            metadata: {
              description: t.description,
              subagent_type: t.subagent_type,
            },
          })

          const agent = await Agent.get(t.subagent_type)
          if (!agent) {
            states.set(t.id, { status: "failed", error: `Unknown agent type: ${t.subagent_type}` })
            resolvers.get(t.id)!.resolve()
            release?.()
            return
          }

          states.set(t.id, { status: "running" })

          const hasTaskPermission = agent.permission.some((rule) => rule.permission === "task")
          const hasTodoWritePermission = agent.permission.some((rule) => rule.permission === "todowrite")
        } catch (err) {
          states.set(t.id, {
            status: "failed",
            error: err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err),
          })
          resolvers.get(t.id)!.resolve()
          release?.()
          return
        }
```

This test name claims it validates the minimum-tasks constraint, but it only checks that `TeamTool.init()` resolves. To actually cover the `.min(1)` schema, add an assertion that calling `execute` with `{ tasks: [] }` (or invalid args) rejects with a validation error, similar to how other tool tests exercise schema failures.
```suggestion
  test("parameters schema validates minimum tasks", async () => {
    await using tmp = await tmpdir({
      config: {
        agent: {
          explore: {
            description: "Explore agent",
            mode: "subagent",
          },
        },
      },
    })

    await Instance.provide({
      directory: tmp.path,
      fn: async () => {
        const build = await Agent.get("build")
        const tool = await TeamTool.init({ agent: build })

        const result = tool.execute(
          {
            tasks: [],
          },
          {} as any,
        )

        await expect(result).rejects.toThrow()
      },
    })
```

